      <p>
        All products are supplied strictly for laboratory research and development. The buyer
        confirms they will not use products for human or veterinary purposes, diagnosis, treatment,
        prevention, personal use, or household use, and that they are responsible for determining
        whether purchase, import, possession, and use are permitted for their institution and
        destination.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Orders and Pricing</h2>
      <p>
        Product and pricing information is provided in the current price list available for download
        on this website. Prices are per box (10 vials per box unless stated otherwise) and are subject
        to confirmation in the quotation or invoice. Quotations are valid for the period stated in
        them; where no period is stated, 30 days. Prices exclude shipping and any destination-country
        duties unless explicitly included. An order is confirmed when we issue a written confirmation
        or invoice; until then, a request is not a binding order on either side.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payment methods are communicated with the quotation and may include bank transfer or other
        agreed channels. You are responsible for checking the amount, method, network where
        applicable, and destination before payment. Ownership of goods passes to the buyer upon full
        payment. Where a deposit is agreed for custom synthesis or OEM programs, its terms are stated
        in the quotation.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Quality and Documentation</h2>
      <p>
        Every batch ships with a Certificate of Analysis covering HPLC purity, mass spectrometry
        identity, peptide content, and other batch-specific data. Batch release records can be
        verified online through the <a href="/coa/">COA lookup</a> using the verification code on the
        product label. If a product is shown by an accredited third-party laboratory to deviate
        materially from its COA, we will replace it or refund the purchase price at our discretion,
        provided the claim is made within 30 days of receipt and the product remains sealed and
        properly stored. Research-grade production is not represented as pharmaceutical GMP
        certification.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Shipping</h2>
      <p>
        Shipping methods, timelines, and responsibilities are set out in the
        <a href="/shipping/">Shipping Policy</a>. Delivery and product issues are handled under that
        policy and this section 7.
